config BR2_PACKAGE_GLIBC_COMPAT
	bool "glibc-compat"
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_MUSL
	help
	  ABI shim for vendor binaries linked against libc.so.6 (glibc) that
	  must run on a musl rootfs. Provides a libglibc-compat.so with the
	  glibc-only entry points (__xstat, __isoc99_sscanf, ...) that musl
	  does not export, plus rootfs symlinks for libc.so.6 / libm.so.6 /
	  ld-linux.so.3 -> musl libc.

	  Used by Hi3520DV200 (vendor MPP for V200 only ships glibc-linked
	  .so, while glibc cannot run on the SoC's 3.0.8 kernel) and by the
	  SigmaStar infinity3 (MSC313E) SDK libs.

	  The executable that loads the vendor libs links -lglibc-compat
	  ahead of libc: musl has its own __xstat family, and the first
	  library in load order wins. Hi3520DV200 SDK builds also link
	  -lglibc-compat-static, whose mmap guesses the caller's off_t width.

	  A call neither can bridge for both ABIs at once is redirected per
	  vendor library at install time with rename-import.py, to a
	  glibc-compat wrapper of the same name length: lseek -> lse32, and
	  on infinity3 mmap -> mm32 (a 32-bit off_t). Those wrappers live in
	  libglibc-compat.so, so any executable that loads the infinity3
	  vendor libraries (libmi, libMTE_LINUX, libCam*, libOMX_*, ...)
	  must link -lglibc-compat, or it fails to load with an unresolved
	  mm32.
